1
00:00:01,333 --> 00:00:02,666
[circuits crackling]

2
00:00:02,666 --> 00:00:06,500
[♪♪♪]

3
00:00:14,625 --> 00:00:16,666
[automated voice, over P.A.
Please have your ID ready

4
00:00:16,666 --> 00:00:18,125
for your new household battery.

5
00:00:18,125 --> 00:00:19,750
We are low on inventory,

6
00:00:19,750 --> 00:00:20,833
so not everyone in line

7
00:00:20,833 --> 00:00:22,000
will be fortunate enough

8
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:25,750
to get a replacement
at this time. [crowd groaning]

9
00:00:25,750 --> 00:00:29,083
Well, Percival did ask us
to conserve energy.

10
00:00:29,083 --> 00:00:32,291
I bet I could make it
another day or two if I had to.

11
00:00:32,291 --> 00:00:33,375
Wasn't like this

12
00:00:33,375 --> 00:00:35,041
when Empress Beatrix
was in charge,

13
00:00:35,041 --> 00:00:36,333
that's all I'm sayin'.

14
00:00:36,333 --> 00:00:38,958
Beatrix was torturing dragons
for power!

15
00:00:38,958 --> 00:00:41,208
Which was terrible, of course.

16
00:00:41,208 --> 00:00:43,291
Just didn't have
an energy crisis before,

17
00:00:43,291 --> 00:00:44,708
is all I'm sayin'.

18
00:00:44,708 --> 00:00:48,833
Starting a new government
and infrastructure is not easy.

19
00:00:48,833 --> 00:00:50,583
[energy fritzing]

20
00:00:50,583 --> 00:00:52,333
[groaning]

21
00:00:52,333 --> 00:00:53,416
[crowd grumbling]

22
00:00:53,416 --> 00:00:54,875
Seriously?

23
00:00:54,875 --> 00:00:57,291
Ugh, another blackout?

24
00:00:57,291 --> 00:00:59,333
[electricity crackling]

25
00:01:03,333 --> 00:01:05,958
Third blackout this week!

26
00:01:05,958 --> 00:01:08,625
Our temporary solves
clearly aren't doing enough.

27
00:01:08,625 --> 00:01:10,708
[sighing] Because this old grid

28
00:01:10,708 --> 00:01:12,833
is designed for dragon energy.

29
00:01:12,833 --> 00:01:15,208
We need the time
for a complete conversion,

30
00:01:15,208 --> 00:01:17,041
all while running streetlights,

31
00:01:17,041 --> 00:01:18,583
public transportation,

32
00:01:18,583 --> 00:01:19,666
the Energy Barrier--

33
00:01:19,666 --> 00:01:21,833
That's it!
The Energy Barrier!

34
00:01:21,833 --> 00:01:25,750
That barrier is a leftover
from Empress Beatrix.

35
00:01:25,750 --> 00:01:28,125
Let's reroute that power
for the people's energy.

36
00:01:28,125 --> 00:01:30,208
But with the Claws gone,

37
00:01:30,208 --> 00:01:31,500
using that barrier

38
00:01:31,500 --> 00:01:33,958
is Imperium's
only line of defense.

39
00:01:33,958 --> 00:01:36,041
Who are we
defending ourselves from?

40
00:01:36,041 --> 00:01:38,083
This is an era of peace!

41
00:01:38,083 --> 00:01:39,291
Shut it down!

42
00:01:47,166 --> 00:01:48,583
[crowd cheering]

43
00:01:48,583 --> 00:01:51,125
Ah, looks like
that did the trick.

44
00:01:51,125 --> 00:01:52,958
[crowd screaming in panic]

45
00:01:52,958 --> 00:01:55,375
[screaming]

46
00:01:57,500 --> 00:01:58,833
What is that thing?

47
00:01:58,833 --> 00:02:00,333
[tentacles whipping]

48
00:02:01,500 --> 00:02:03,541
♪ Lost in the unknown ♪

49
00:02:03,541 --> 00:02:04,708
♪ So much to see ♪

50
00:02:04,708 --> 00:02:07,750
♪ Jump up, kick back
whip around and spin ♪

51
00:02:07,750 --> 00:02:09,541
♪ Together we will rise ♪

52
00:02:09,541 --> 00:02:10,791
♪ Whip around and spin ♪

53
00:02:10,791 --> 00:02:12,375
♪ Together we will rise ♪

54
00:02:12,375 --> 00:02:14,291
♪ For what's right ♪♪

55
00:02:26,541 --> 00:02:28,500
[groaning weakly]

56
00:02:28,500 --> 00:02:29,791
Come on, Riyu,

57
00:02:29,791 --> 00:02:32,125
pull through.

58
00:02:32,125 --> 00:02:33,958
[labored breathing]

59
00:02:33,958 --> 00:02:35,041
[sipping weakly]

60
00:02:35,041 --> 00:02:36,458
He took a direct hit

61
00:02:36,458 --> 00:02:38,666
of whatever that monster
was blasting.

62
00:02:38,666 --> 00:02:41,541
I've never seen a dragon
survive such a thing,

63
00:02:41,541 --> 00:02:44,333
and I've seen a lot of dragons
in battle.

64
00:02:44,333 --> 00:02:46,416
He's always been
a special dragon.

65
00:02:46,416 --> 00:02:49,375
Do you think he could eat?

66
00:02:49,375 --> 00:02:52,125
We make delicious
Umbrasylvan wheatcakes.

67
00:02:52,125 --> 00:02:54,041
It's worth a shot, I guess.

68
00:02:54,041 --> 00:02:56,875
Thank--Thank you
for all your help.

69
00:02:56,875 --> 00:02:58,125
Thank you.

70
00:02:58,125 --> 00:03:00,333
That dragon is a hero.

71
00:03:00,333 --> 00:03:02,125
He saved our village--

72
00:03:02,125 --> 00:03:04,583
You still tending
to that beast?

73
00:03:04,583 --> 00:03:06,375
Riyu is not a beast,

74
00:03:06,375 --> 00:03:08,333
he's one of us, a Ninja,

75
00:03:08,333 --> 00:03:09,958
and you owe him your life,

76
00:03:09,958 --> 00:03:11,708
you uptight wad.

77
00:03:11,708 --> 00:03:13,375
By jove, I didn't realize

78
00:03:13,375 --> 00:03:16,208
this subject would lead
to such crass name-calling.

79
00:03:16,208 --> 00:03:17,333
Anyway,

80
00:03:17,333 --> 00:03:18,916
I just wanted to let
everyone know

81
00:03:18,916 --> 00:03:22,541
that monster is now
safely contained in our airship

82
00:03:22,541 --> 00:03:24,625
for future study and display.

83
00:03:24,625 --> 00:03:26,666
In case you were wondering.

84
00:03:27,666 --> 00:03:30,750
I-I'll just...
see myself out then.

85
00:03:30,750 --> 00:03:31,750
The Numbness.

86
00:03:31,750 --> 00:03:32,750
The what?

87
00:03:32,750 --> 00:03:34,166
[Wyldfyre]
When dragons are exposed

88
00:03:34,166 --> 00:03:35,708
to a dangerous substance--

89
00:03:35,708 --> 00:03:37,000
poisonous leffberries,

90
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:38,416
the spray
of a saber-toothed eel,

91
00:03:38,416 --> 00:03:39,666
stuff like that--

92
00:03:39,666 --> 00:03:42,541
they can get something
we call "The Numbness".

93
00:03:42,541 --> 00:03:44,875
It's... usually fatal.

94
00:03:44,875 --> 00:03:45,833
Usually?

95
00:03:45,833 --> 00:03:47,291
I heard stories
of Dragon Elders

96
00:03:47,291 --> 00:03:48,708
curing the Numbness

97
00:03:48,708 --> 00:03:51,666
by converting a small amount
of whatever caused the problem

98
00:03:51,666 --> 00:03:52,916
into an antidote.

99
00:03:52,916 --> 00:03:54,125
Convert how?

100
00:03:54,125 --> 00:03:55,125
I don't know!

101
00:03:55,125 --> 00:03:56,500
I'm just telling you
what I heard.

102
00:03:56,500 --> 00:03:58,833
Do I look like a dragon doctor?

103
00:03:58,833 --> 00:04:00,583
So converting venom

104
00:04:00,583 --> 00:04:02,375
could help his body's
natural defenses?

105
00:04:02,375 --> 00:04:03,916
But he wasn't poisoned
by the venom

106
00:04:03,916 --> 00:04:05,125
of a buck-toothed eel--

107
00:04:05,125 --> 00:04:06,458
Saber-toothed.

108
00:04:06,458 --> 00:04:08,666
--he was blasted by a monster!

109
00:04:08,666 --> 00:04:10,833
Yeah, but that monster

110
00:04:10,833 --> 00:04:13,333
looked like it was made
out of Elemental Energy.

111
00:04:13,333 --> 00:04:14,416
So?

112
00:04:14,416 --> 00:04:16,500
Look, before you joined
the team,

113
00:04:16,500 --> 00:04:18,958
I didn't think
I had my own powers.

114
00:04:18,958 --> 00:04:20,875
I thought Riyu gave them to me.

115
00:04:20,875 --> 00:04:22,375
Weird, but okay.

116
00:04:22,375 --> 00:04:24,250
Every time
I got a spark of power,

117
00:04:24,250 --> 00:04:27,000
I could feel the energy
rolling through me,

118
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:28,333
like a wave.

119
00:04:28,333 --> 00:04:30,291
[Riyu groaning softly]

120
00:04:30,291 --> 00:04:34,000
Like a substance
that can affect the body.

121
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:37,625
Oh, so we reverse
that monster's energy somehow,

122
00:04:37,625 --> 00:04:39,875
and give it back to Riyu?

123
00:04:39,875 --> 00:04:41,500
Oh, so when she says it,
it sounds smart?

124
00:04:41,500 --> 00:04:42,500
[blows a raspberry]

125
00:04:42,500 --> 00:04:43,958
I just need to create something

126
00:04:43,958 --> 00:04:46,333
that can convert
that kind of energy.

127
00:04:46,333 --> 00:04:48,000
[Riyu groaning softly]

128
00:04:52,458 --> 00:04:54,666
[Freya] We don't have much
advanced technology

129
00:04:54,666 --> 00:04:55,833
in Umbrasylvis,

130
00:04:55,833 --> 00:04:58,583
but what little we have gathered

131
00:04:58,583 --> 00:05:01,166
is basically all here.

132
00:05:01,166 --> 00:05:04,666
I hope it helps you save
the hero dragon.

133
00:05:04,666 --> 00:05:05,958
Oh, wow, thank you.

134
00:05:07,291 --> 00:05:08,791
[cracking joints, exhaling]

135
00:05:09,708 --> 00:05:11,666
[energy sputtering]

136
00:05:16,208 --> 00:05:17,458
Ugh.

137
00:05:17,458 --> 00:05:18,625
How am I going to
get to do this

138
00:05:18,625 --> 00:05:20,625
with our powers on the fritz?

139
00:05:22,375 --> 00:05:23,416
[exhaling]

140
00:05:27,125 --> 00:05:28,708
[energy sputtering]

141
00:05:28,708 --> 00:05:30,083
[monster roaring]

142
00:05:30,083 --> 00:05:30,958
Whoa!

143
00:05:32,250 --> 00:05:33,291
[monster hissing]

144
00:05:33,291 --> 00:05:35,000
-Hup!
-H'yah!

145
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:36,916
[grunting]

146
00:05:37,958 --> 00:05:39,833
[monsters growling]

147
00:05:41,916 --> 00:05:42,791
H'yah! Y'ah!

148
00:05:42,791 --> 00:05:44,083
Ah!

149
00:05:44,083 --> 00:05:45,791
[groaning in pain]

150
00:05:45,791 --> 00:05:47,166
Y'ah!

151
00:05:47,166 --> 00:05:48,208
[gasping]

152
00:05:48,208 --> 00:05:49,916
[monsters growling]

153
00:05:49,916 --> 00:05:52,000
[snarling]

154
00:05:57,041 --> 00:05:58,875
[rotors whirring]

155
00:06:07,875 --> 00:06:08,708
H'yah!

156
00:06:08,708 --> 00:06:10,083
[♪♪♪]

157
00:06:10,083 --> 00:06:11,750
[Zane] Surprise-surprise!

158
00:06:12,750 --> 00:06:13,583
H'ah!

159
00:06:15,791 --> 00:06:17,291
[Lloyd] Zane?

160
00:06:17,291 --> 00:06:18,541
How did you find us?

161
00:06:21,083 --> 00:06:22,500
[Zane] When my powers
got all janky...

162
00:06:24,875 --> 00:06:26,958
...Pixal and I split up
to search for you all.

163
00:06:26,958 --> 00:06:28,708
"J-Janky"?

164
00:06:28,708 --> 00:06:30,458
[Zane]
I say "janky" now, Lloyd.

165
00:06:30,458 --> 00:06:31,750
H'yah!

166
00:06:32,750 --> 00:06:33,750
I was flying over these woods

167
00:06:33,750 --> 00:06:35,833
and heard sounds of battle,

168
00:06:35,833 --> 00:06:37,916
and guess who was
right at the center of it?

169
00:06:41,083 --> 00:06:43,083
And I see you're dealing
with Elemental Monsters

170
00:06:43,083 --> 00:06:44,500
in this land as well.

171
00:06:44,500 --> 00:06:45,541
H'yah!

172
00:06:45,541 --> 00:06:46,541
Oof!

173
00:06:46,541 --> 00:06:48,458
They're in other places, too?

174
00:06:48,458 --> 00:06:49,416
They're all-- Ugh!

175
00:06:49,416 --> 00:06:50,750
--over the place,

176
00:06:50,750 --> 00:06:52,291
and nearly unbeatable!

177
00:06:52,291 --> 00:06:53,958
H'yah!

178
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:56,500
[energy sputtering]

179
00:06:56,500 --> 00:06:59,125
[disembodied whispering]

180
00:07:05,666 --> 00:07:07,541
[♪♪♪]

181
00:07:12,166 --> 00:07:13,625
Ugh!

182
00:07:15,333 --> 00:07:16,666
[Lloyd] Yes!

183
00:07:17,875 --> 00:07:18,875
H'yah!

184
00:07:25,416 --> 00:07:26,916
Powers are back again!

185
00:07:26,916 --> 00:07:28,166
Again?

186
00:07:32,666 --> 00:07:33,750
Y'ah!

187
00:07:39,041 --> 00:07:39,916
H'yah!

188
00:07:39,916 --> 00:07:41,250
Hup! Y'ah!

189
00:07:44,250 --> 00:07:45,875
H'ah!

190
00:07:50,250 --> 00:07:52,125
[Lloyd roaring]

191
00:07:56,125 --> 00:07:57,541
Did we win?

192
00:08:00,375 --> 00:08:02,791
I can sense trace readings
of their energies,

193
00:08:02,791 --> 00:08:04,875
yet I think they've moved on,

194
00:08:04,875 --> 00:08:07,583
but why are
our powers stable here?

195
00:08:07,583 --> 00:08:09,250
[Lloyd] It won't last.

196
00:08:09,250 --> 00:08:10,750
[energy sputtering]

197
00:08:10,750 --> 00:08:12,083
I see.

198
00:08:12,083 --> 00:08:13,375
What a bummer.

199
00:08:13,375 --> 00:08:16,208
Zane, did you...
reprogram yourself or something?

200
00:08:16,208 --> 00:08:18,833
"Bummer" didn't use to be
part of your vocab.

201
00:08:18,833 --> 00:08:21,916
My time with Pixal
did wonders for my disposition.

202
00:08:21,916 --> 00:08:24,416
Some might say
I'm more "chill,"

203
00:08:24,416 --> 00:08:26,791
and when did you
rejoin the team, Arin?

204
00:08:26,791 --> 00:08:28,125
[chuckling] Oh, man,

205
00:08:28,125 --> 00:08:30,166
you've missed a lot!

206
00:08:30,166 --> 00:08:32,958
[Lloyd] Including the reason
our powers are messed up.

207
00:08:32,958 --> 00:08:36,291
We, uh, did something
that angered the Source Dragons,

208
00:08:36,291 --> 00:08:38,166
so half of them
pulled their powers

209
00:08:38,166 --> 00:08:39,666
from the Merged Lands.

210
00:08:39,666 --> 00:08:41,166
I skip one adventure,

211
00:08:41,166 --> 00:08:43,625
and the entire world
turns to chaos.

212
00:08:43,625 --> 00:08:46,083
Hey, we're searching
for a way to fix it all.

213
00:08:46,083 --> 00:08:48,541
Any interest
in helping us find something

214
00:08:48,541 --> 00:08:50,375
called
the Temple of the Green Ninja?

215
00:08:53,041 --> 00:08:54,583
[printer whirring]

216
00:08:57,083 --> 00:08:58,125
[Kai] So, what even is

217
00:08:58,125 --> 00:09:00,458
a "Department
of Vacation Simulation"?

218
00:09:00,458 --> 00:09:02,791
[Jay] Administration employees
earn vacation days,

219
00:09:02,791 --> 00:09:05,291
but aren't allowed
to actually go anywhere...

220
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:13,083
...so we--
I mean, they--

221
00:09:13,083 --> 00:09:16,208
go up and sit
in Vacation Simulator chairs.

222
00:09:16,208 --> 00:09:17,208
It tricks your brain

223
00:09:17,208 --> 00:09:18,708
into thinking
you're at the beach,

224
00:09:18,708 --> 00:09:21,166
the mountains,
an amusement park, whatever.

225
00:09:21,166 --> 00:09:22,916
[Nya] So the Agents like that?

226
00:09:22,916 --> 00:09:24,750
A Fake-Cation?

227
00:09:24,750 --> 00:09:27,291
[Jay laughing] A "Fake-Cation!"

228
00:09:27,291 --> 00:09:29,083
I should've thought of that one!

229
00:09:29,083 --> 00:09:31,875
The Agents here
don't even know it's weird.

230
00:09:31,875 --> 00:09:33,750
Land of Madness, remember?

231
00:09:33,750 --> 00:09:35,583
[Nya] So how do we get there?

232
00:09:35,583 --> 00:09:37,333
[Kai] Uh, the elevator, duh!

233
00:09:37,333 --> 00:09:40,166
[Jay] That's how Agents
go up and down floors!

234
00:09:40,166 --> 00:09:41,166
Don't be ridiculous.

235
00:09:41,166 --> 00:09:42,958
[Kai] Don't have
to bite my head off.

236
00:09:42,958 --> 00:09:44,916
Like you never had
any bad ideas.

237
00:09:44,916 --> 00:09:46,666
[Jay] As far as I remember,
no, never.

238
00:09:46,666 --> 00:09:47,791
[Kai scoffing]

239
00:09:47,791 --> 00:09:49,625
[chuckling] When you get
your memories back,

240
00:09:49,625 --> 00:09:52,541
you're in for a rude awakening.

241
00:09:52,541 --> 00:09:54,208
<i>[voice over P.A.]</i>
<i>Attention all Agents,</i>

242
00:09:54,208 --> 00:09:55,333
<i>there are three Ninja</i>

243
00:09:55,333 --> 00:09:56,708
<i>within the confines</i>
<i>of the building.</i>

244
00:09:56,708 --> 00:09:59,708
<i>Please get</i>
<i>to the nearest safety station--</i>

245
00:09:59,708 --> 00:10:00,916
[Jay] "Safety Station"?

246
00:10:00,916 --> 00:10:03,541
<i>--because the highly efficient</i>
<i>Robo-Eliminators</i>

247
00:10:03,541 --> 00:10:05,750
<i>are now online.</i>

248
00:10:06,916 --> 00:10:07,958
[groaning softly]

249
00:10:09,958 --> 00:10:11,791
Our family doesn't have much,

250
00:10:11,791 --> 00:10:14,500
but we made this
with what we have.

251
00:10:14,500 --> 00:10:15,333
Thank you.

252
00:10:19,916 --> 00:10:21,875
Gave up on your powers?

253
00:10:21,875 --> 00:10:23,166
I built inventions by hand

254
00:10:23,166 --> 00:10:25,958
long before I even knew
what an elemental power was.

255
00:10:25,958 --> 00:10:27,875
He's sinking deeper
into the Numbness.

256
00:10:27,875 --> 00:10:30,125
Whatever you're doing, Sora,
do it faster.

257
00:10:31,625 --> 00:10:33,000
Got it!

258
00:10:33,000 --> 00:10:35,291
I should be
a motivational speaker.

259
00:10:35,291 --> 00:10:37,250
Time to collect
some Elemental Monster energy.

260
00:10:37,250 --> 00:10:38,500
Let's go!

261
00:10:39,958 --> 00:10:42,208
[tube suction hissing]

262
00:10:44,958 --> 00:10:46,166
What the--?

263
00:10:52,375 --> 00:10:54,458
[beating drum]

264
00:11:03,416 --> 00:11:04,916
A speech is in order!

265
00:11:04,916 --> 00:11:06,166
[clearing throat]
I'll give it.

266
00:11:06,166 --> 00:11:07,416
[drum roll]

267
00:11:07,416 --> 00:11:09,916
Members of
the Umbrasylvian Expedition,

268
00:11:09,916 --> 00:11:12,166
congratulations on my--

269
00:11:12,166 --> 00:11:14,291
our-- great victory!

270
00:11:14,291 --> 00:11:17,791
Defeating an unknown monster
in open combat

271
00:11:17,791 --> 00:11:20,333
and saving an innocent town!

272
00:11:20,333 --> 00:11:21,291
Huzzah!

273
00:11:21,291 --> 00:11:22,291
What?

274
00:11:22,291 --> 00:11:23,500
Riyu did that!

275
00:11:23,500 --> 00:11:25,708
Yes, yes, yes,
the dragon was helpful,

276
00:11:25,708 --> 00:11:27,833
and certainly deserves
Honorable Mention,

277
00:11:27,833 --> 00:11:29,000
but thankfully,

278
00:11:29,000 --> 00:11:30,000
we were the ones

279
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:31,541
who contained the creature,

280
00:11:31,541 --> 00:11:33,208
rendering it safe.

281
00:11:33,208 --> 00:11:35,166
I built that containment unit.

282
00:11:35,166 --> 00:11:37,416
And you did an excellent job...

283
00:11:37,416 --> 00:11:38,583
of obeying me,

284
00:11:38,583 --> 00:11:40,166
since I led you do to it.

285
00:11:40,166 --> 00:11:41,833
-What!
-[sighing]

286
00:11:41,833 --> 00:11:43,875
And now, thanks to my--

287
00:11:43,875 --> 00:11:45,208
our skill,

288
00:11:45,208 --> 00:11:46,291
we'll transport

289
00:11:46,291 --> 00:11:49,750
this unparalleled
scientific discovery

290
00:11:49,750 --> 00:11:50,958
to Ninjago,

291
00:11:50,958 --> 00:11:54,833
where it can be put on display
for the benefit of all...

292
00:11:54,833 --> 00:11:56,666
and the profit of me--

293
00:11:56,666 --> 00:11:58,000
uh-- us!

294
00:11:58,000 --> 00:11:59,208
Huzzah!

295
00:11:59,208 --> 00:12:01,333
Ugh! We don't have time
for this!

296
00:12:01,333 --> 00:12:03,750
[device powering up]

297
00:12:03,750 --> 00:12:05,041
[snarling]

298
00:12:07,875 --> 00:12:08,875
Excuse me.

299
00:12:08,875 --> 00:12:10,208
I don't know what you're doing,

300
00:12:10,208 --> 00:12:12,958
but that's property
of the Explorers Club,

301
00:12:12,958 --> 00:12:15,750
and I forbid you
to interfere with it in any way.

302
00:12:15,750 --> 00:12:16,833
[Frak] Dad?

303
00:12:16,833 --> 00:12:18,416
We need this right now.

304
00:12:18,416 --> 00:12:20,333
It could save Riyu's life.

305
00:12:20,333 --> 00:12:22,500
Well, why didn't you say so?

306
00:12:22,500 --> 00:12:24,291
Well, in that case,

307
00:12:24,291 --> 00:12:25,625
we should enter negotiations

308
00:12:25,625 --> 00:12:26,875
on how much to charge you
for access to--

309
00:12:26,875 --> 00:12:27,958
[device beeping]

310
00:12:28,916 --> 00:12:31,416
[monster grunting]

311
00:12:33,083 --> 00:12:34,833
Done.

312
00:12:34,833 --> 00:12:36,875
[sputtering] Okay, yes, uh,
you were only able to do that

313
00:12:36,875 --> 00:12:39,291
because I gave you permission.

314
00:12:39,291 --> 00:12:40,666
Permission granted!

315
00:12:40,666 --> 00:12:42,791
[Zane] ...so I said to Pixal,

316
00:12:42,791 --> 00:12:44,041
how was I to know

317
00:12:44,041 --> 00:12:46,000
the Ampfedrox people
incubate their offspring

318
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:47,750
in containers
that look like teacups?

319
00:12:47,750 --> 00:12:50,416
She laughed
for 45 seconds straight,

320
00:12:50,416 --> 00:12:53,083
and I laughed for 52 seconds.

321
00:12:53,083 --> 00:12:54,791
It was quite an experience.

322
00:12:54,791 --> 00:12:56,291
[Arin and Euphrasia laughing]

323
00:12:56,291 --> 00:12:59,000
I'm... lost.

324
00:12:59,000 --> 00:13:00,833
Let's take a break here.

325
00:13:00,833 --> 00:13:02,083
Try to get our bearings.

326
00:13:02,083 --> 00:13:03,666
[Arin] Sounds good to me.

327
00:13:08,166 --> 00:13:10,541
[♪♪♪]

328
00:13:11,833 --> 00:13:14,250
Remember when I was
too scared to admit

329
00:13:14,250 --> 00:13:15,333
I had powers?

330
00:13:15,333 --> 00:13:17,083
How could I forget?

331
00:13:17,083 --> 00:13:19,250
Almost got eaten
by a giant octopus thing.

332
00:13:19,250 --> 00:13:21,666
But now that my powers
don't work,

333
00:13:21,666 --> 00:13:24,416
I'm scared that I can't protect
the Cloud Kingdom anymore.

334
00:13:24,416 --> 00:13:27,458
There's more to self-defense
than powers.

335
00:13:27,458 --> 00:13:30,416
Trust me, it's something
I'm very familiar with.

336
00:13:30,416 --> 00:13:34,541
Yeah, but you're like
a Spinjitzu genius.

337
00:13:34,541 --> 00:13:35,875
I could never do that.

338
00:13:35,875 --> 00:13:39,083
I taught myself
basic Spinjitzu alone.

339
00:13:39,083 --> 00:13:41,125
Maybe I could teach you?

340
00:13:41,125 --> 00:13:42,208
Really?

341
00:13:42,208 --> 00:13:43,666
If you'd like me to.

342
00:13:46,666 --> 00:13:49,958
Okay, it starts with balance.

343
00:13:49,958 --> 00:13:51,916
Try this first position.

344
00:13:51,916 --> 00:13:52,916
H'ah!

345
00:13:54,375 --> 00:13:56,416
[forest birds warbling]

346
00:13:56,416 --> 00:13:57,750
Why are you squinting?

347
00:13:57,750 --> 00:14:01,333
Trying to sense
where this temple could be.

348
00:14:01,333 --> 00:14:03,041
By squinting?

349
00:14:03,041 --> 00:14:06,250
By concentrating.

350
00:14:06,250 --> 00:14:07,250
Ugh!

351
00:14:07,250 --> 00:14:09,625
I don't even know
what I'm even doing!

352
00:14:09,625 --> 00:14:11,916
Maybe your doubts
are clouding your senses.

353
00:14:11,916 --> 00:14:13,333
Don't focus on them.

354
00:14:13,333 --> 00:14:16,416
How do I just
not focus on doubts?

355
00:14:16,416 --> 00:14:17,958
Sketch.

356
00:14:17,958 --> 00:14:19,625
The forest, the rocks,

357
00:14:19,625 --> 00:14:21,083
anything that comes to mind.

358
00:14:24,375 --> 00:14:26,666
When did you get into art?

359
00:14:26,666 --> 00:14:28,125
Art is like...

360
00:14:28,125 --> 00:14:29,250
the opposite of you.

361
00:14:29,250 --> 00:14:31,166
It's a way
of processing problems

362
00:14:31,166 --> 00:14:33,291
without the constraints
of logic-based thinking.

363
00:14:33,291 --> 00:14:35,583
Trying to get away from logic?

364
00:14:35,583 --> 00:14:36,625
You?

365
00:14:36,625 --> 00:14:38,625
Logic is an important
and powerful tool,

366
00:14:38,625 --> 00:14:41,041
but I've learned
being too focused on it

367
00:14:41,041 --> 00:14:42,750
can get in the way
of creative insights.

368
00:14:42,750 --> 00:14:44,041
Wow, Zane.

369
00:14:44,041 --> 00:14:45,291
This voyage with Pixal

370
00:14:45,291 --> 00:14:47,333
really did have
an impact on you.

371
00:14:47,333 --> 00:14:48,875
It did.

372
00:14:48,875 --> 00:14:51,791
Love is also an important
and powerful tool.

373
00:14:51,791 --> 00:14:53,708
[disembodied whispering]

374
00:14:53,708 --> 00:14:55,166
If it helps,

375
00:14:55,166 --> 00:14:57,958
think of drawing
as a form of meditation.

376
00:14:57,958 --> 00:15:00,416
Pencil to the paper,

377
00:15:00,416 --> 00:15:02,083
breathing.

378
00:15:02,083 --> 00:15:04,166
[inhaling]

379
00:15:04,166 --> 00:15:06,000
[disembodied whispering grows]

380
00:15:13,500 --> 00:15:14,500
Huh.

381
00:15:14,500 --> 00:15:16,500
I think it worked.

382
00:15:16,500 --> 00:15:17,791
[♪♪♪]

383
00:15:22,208 --> 00:15:23,500
Please work.

384
00:15:26,291 --> 00:15:27,291
[injection hissing]

385
00:15:27,291 --> 00:15:28,333
Why didn't you say anything?

386
00:15:28,333 --> 00:15:29,375
What?

387
00:15:29,375 --> 00:15:30,666
Your dad,

388
00:15:30,666 --> 00:15:31,916
he took credit for everything,

389
00:15:31,916 --> 00:15:32,958
and you just let him do it.

390
00:15:32,958 --> 00:15:34,166
Look,

391
00:15:34,166 --> 00:15:35,791
no one knows
how annoying he is

392
00:15:35,791 --> 00:15:36,750
more than I do,

393
00:15:36,750 --> 00:15:39,375
but growing up, in my house,

394
00:15:39,375 --> 00:15:40,625
you didn't ever
disagree with him.

395
00:15:40,625 --> 00:15:42,416
Speaking your mind?

396
00:15:42,416 --> 00:15:43,708
Not acceptable.

397
00:15:43,708 --> 00:15:45,916
But you're not a kid anymore.

398
00:15:45,916 --> 00:15:47,416
No.

399
00:15:47,416 --> 00:15:49,083
No, I'm not.

400
00:15:51,541 --> 00:15:53,083
[groaning]

401
00:15:54,333 --> 00:15:55,541
Well?

402
00:15:58,125 --> 00:15:59,083
No change.

403
00:16:04,791 --> 00:16:06,625
[♪♪♪]

404
00:16:15,541 --> 00:16:16,958
<i>[Eliminator 1] Ninja located?</i>

405
00:16:16,958 --> 00:16:18,666
<i>[Eliminator 2] Negative.</i>

406
00:16:18,666 --> 00:16:21,041
<i>[Eliminator 1] Ninja</i>
<i>must be located with efficiency</i>

407
00:16:21,041 --> 00:16:22,000
<i>for purposes of...</i>

408
00:16:22,000 --> 00:16:24,750
<i>elimination.</i>

409
00:16:24,750 --> 00:16:26,333
<i>[together]</i>
<i>Eliminate! Eliminate!</i>

410
00:16:27,416 --> 00:16:28,583
<i>Eliminate! Eliminate!</i>

411
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:31,375
[Kai] Uh, those things

412
00:16:31,375 --> 00:16:33,125
are supposed to be
highly efficient?

413
00:16:33,125 --> 00:16:35,041
[Jay] For this place,
absolutely.

414
00:16:35,041 --> 00:16:36,291
Maybe they brought in

415
00:16:36,291 --> 00:16:38,625
an outside
Efficiency Consultant?

416
00:16:38,625 --> 00:16:40,791
We should be clear
if we just go around--

417
00:16:40,791 --> 00:16:41,750
Ooh.

418
00:16:42,666 --> 00:16:44,000
Funny thing!

419
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:46,166
Sometimes people think
we're Ninja,

420
00:16:46,166 --> 00:16:48,250
but we're just Ninja cosplayers.

421
00:16:48,250 --> 00:16:49,625
[chuckling awkwardly]

422
00:16:49,625 --> 00:16:52,500
<i>[Eliminator 3]</i>
<i>Sneaky Ninja lie... detected.</i>

423
00:16:52,500 --> 00:16:54,041
<i>Eliminate! Eliminate!</i>

424
00:16:54,041 --> 00:16:55,625
[Sora] He just...

425
00:16:55,625 --> 00:16:57,250
he needs to be okay.

426
00:16:57,250 --> 00:16:59,833
This little guy changed my life.

427
00:16:59,833 --> 00:17:00,833
Little?

428
00:17:00,833 --> 00:17:03,083
He'll always be
a little guy to me.

429
00:17:04,083 --> 00:17:05,375
[Riyu's breath wheezing]

430
00:17:05,375 --> 00:17:06,541
No...

431
00:17:06,541 --> 00:17:09,291
[wheezing]

432
00:17:09,291 --> 00:17:11,125
Come on.

433
00:17:11,125 --> 00:17:12,833
Wh-what?

434
00:17:12,833 --> 00:17:14,708
He's not getting better.

435
00:17:14,708 --> 00:17:15,708
Nothing's changing.

436
00:17:15,708 --> 00:17:17,000
You said it would work.

437
00:17:17,000 --> 00:17:18,333
I also said
I'm not a dragon doctor,

438
00:17:18,333 --> 00:17:19,625
remember?

439
00:17:19,625 --> 00:17:22,625
I-I just took a guess
at how much energy he needed.

440
00:17:22,625 --> 00:17:23,666
Maybe he needs more?

441
00:17:23,666 --> 00:17:24,958
We're losing him.

442
00:17:24,958 --> 00:17:27,250
We need to keep trying
until it works.

443
00:17:27,250 --> 00:17:29,041
We'll be right back.

444
00:17:30,916 --> 00:17:32,083
[can rattling]

445
00:17:33,500 --> 00:17:35,000
It's gone.

446
00:17:35,000 --> 00:17:37,458
Someone opened
the Containment Unit

447
00:17:37,458 --> 00:17:38,458
and let it out.

448
00:17:38,458 --> 00:17:39,500
Who would--?

449
00:17:39,500 --> 00:17:40,583
[nearby screaming]

450
00:17:44,583 --> 00:17:45,666
<i>[Eliminator 1] Locate Ninja.</i>

451
00:17:45,666 --> 00:17:47,458
<i>Eliminate!</i>

452
00:17:54,125 --> 00:17:55,791
[Jay] Now!

453
00:17:55,791 --> 00:17:56,791
<i>Eliminate! Eliminate!</i>

454
00:17:56,791 --> 00:17:58,291
H'yah!

455
00:18:00,791 --> 00:18:01,833
[beeping]

456
00:18:01,833 --> 00:18:03,333
H'yah!

457
00:18:08,000 --> 00:18:09,041
[Jay] Nya!

458
00:18:09,041 --> 00:18:10,875
I'm thinking these bots
are overworked!

459
00:18:10,875 --> 00:18:13,916
[Nya] Then it sounds like
they need a vacation!

460
00:18:16,208 --> 00:18:18,375
[bots powering down]

461
00:18:19,458 --> 00:18:20,916
<i>Whee!</i>

462
00:18:22,416 --> 00:18:26,041
So, what Fake-Cation
did we send them on?

463
00:18:26,041 --> 00:18:27,583
Uh...

464
00:18:27,583 --> 00:18:29,750
the Land of Lee, Cavern Five.

465
00:18:29,750 --> 00:18:31,416
Uh, Robots on waterslides?

466
00:18:31,416 --> 00:18:32,416
How does that work?

467
00:18:32,416 --> 00:18:34,291
As much as I'd love to ruminate

468
00:18:34,291 --> 00:18:36,333
on the physics of robots
and water tubes,

469
00:18:36,333 --> 00:18:38,333
we came here for a reason.

470
00:18:39,458 --> 00:18:40,750
Oh...

471
00:18:40,750 --> 00:18:42,916
Agent Donovan wasn't lying.

472
00:18:42,916 --> 00:18:44,000
This equipment

473
00:18:44,000 --> 00:18:46,458
that beams vacations
into people's brains

474
00:18:46,458 --> 00:18:48,166
could be used
to block memories,

475
00:18:48,166 --> 00:18:49,833
in theory.

476
00:18:49,833 --> 00:18:51,083
Not in theory.

477
00:18:51,083 --> 00:18:52,083
I'm proof,

478
00:18:52,083 --> 00:18:53,458
but...

479
00:18:53,458 --> 00:18:54,666
can you reverse it?

480
00:18:54,666 --> 00:18:55,875
Of course she can.

481
00:18:55,875 --> 00:18:57,708
You can, can't you, sis?

482
00:18:57,708 --> 00:18:58,708
Maybe?

483
00:18:58,708 --> 00:19:01,083
What are we waiting for?

484
00:19:01,083 --> 00:19:02,083
Hold it.

485
00:19:02,083 --> 00:19:03,708
This is risky.

486
00:19:03,708 --> 00:19:05,541
I can't guarantee
it's gonna work.

487
00:19:05,541 --> 00:19:06,458
So?

488
00:19:06,458 --> 00:19:08,333
Then I don't get
my memories back?

489
00:19:08,333 --> 00:19:09,250
Big deal.

490
00:19:09,250 --> 00:19:10,500
I already don't have them.

491
00:19:11,375 --> 00:19:12,291
No.

492
00:19:12,291 --> 00:19:13,666
If this fails,

493
00:19:13,666 --> 00:19:15,125
we could damage your brain,

494
00:19:15,125 --> 00:19:17,375
making it impossible for you
to form new memories

495
00:19:17,375 --> 00:19:19,000
ever again.

496
00:19:19,000 --> 00:19:20,875
Like a permanent state
of amnesia?

497
00:19:20,875 --> 00:19:22,750
[Nya] Yes.

498
00:19:24,333 --> 00:19:25,333
Doesn't matter.

499
00:19:25,333 --> 00:19:26,541
Let's do it.

500
00:19:26,541 --> 00:19:28,041
Jay, think this through.

501
00:19:28,041 --> 00:19:30,833
You're here, with us,
back on the team.

502
00:19:30,833 --> 00:19:32,791
You can relearn Spinjitzu.

503
00:19:32,791 --> 00:19:34,875
We can make new memories,

504
00:19:34,875 --> 00:19:36,375
better than the old ones.

505
00:19:36,375 --> 00:19:37,791
He's right.

506
00:19:37,791 --> 00:19:39,291
You're still the Jay I love

507
00:19:39,291 --> 00:19:40,666
even without your memories.

508
00:19:40,666 --> 00:19:43,000
You know why I have to do this.

509
00:19:43,000 --> 00:19:45,041
I had a whole life,

510
00:19:45,041 --> 00:19:47,750
apparently a whole
wonderful life,

511
00:19:47,750 --> 00:19:49,166
with all of you,

512
00:19:49,166 --> 00:19:52,666
and I can't go on another moment
without remembering it.

513
00:19:54,666 --> 00:19:55,916
This might hurt.

514
00:19:57,583 --> 00:19:58,791
[typing rapidly]

515
00:19:58,791 --> 00:20:00,166
[♪♪♪]

516
00:20:06,250 --> 00:20:09,125
[screaming]

517
00:20:09,125 --> 00:20:10,458
Turn it off.

518
00:20:10,458 --> 00:20:11,833
Turn it off!
It's hurting him!

519
00:20:11,833 --> 00:20:13,750
I think this is how it works!

520
00:20:13,750 --> 00:20:14,958
[♪♪♪]

521
00:20:23,916 --> 00:20:25,125
[screaming]

522
00:20:25,125 --> 00:20:27,250
[♪♪♪]

523
00:20:41,291 --> 00:20:42,666
[screaming]

524
00:20:42,666 --> 00:20:43,625
[machine powering down]

525
00:20:43,625 --> 00:20:44,791
Oh no...

526
00:20:44,791 --> 00:20:45,708
Oh no!

527
00:20:47,333 --> 00:20:48,416
[Kai's voice muffled] Jay?

528
00:20:48,416 --> 00:20:49,833
You with us, buddy?

529
00:21:01,625 --> 00:21:02,583
[♪♪♪]

530
00:21:06,000 --> 00:21:07,875
I'll take that as a yes.

531
00:21:07,875 --> 00:21:09,291
[smooching noises]

532
00:21:09,291 --> 00:21:10,416
All right, we get it.

533
00:21:10,416 --> 00:21:11,416
That's enough.

534
00:21:11,416 --> 00:21:12,375
[smooching noises]

535
00:21:12,375 --> 00:21:13,375
Come on, dude, that's my sister!

536
00:21:18,041 --> 00:21:20,625
So he heard whispers,
then drew a map?

537
00:21:20,625 --> 00:21:22,000
I mean, don't get me wrong,

538
00:21:22,000 --> 00:21:23,958
I'm a Writer of Destiny, but...

539
00:21:23,958 --> 00:21:25,500
I'm not sure--

540
00:21:25,500 --> 00:21:26,458
[Lloyd] We're here.

541
00:21:29,583 --> 00:21:30,541
We are?

542
00:21:36,000 --> 00:21:37,750
Whoa!

543
00:21:38,750 --> 00:21:39,708
We are.

544
00:21:41,916 --> 00:21:43,916
[disembodied whispering]

545
00:21:45,000 --> 00:21:45,875
[♪♪♪]

